Hi There.  My name is Greg and I work at Software Sorcery in the tech 
support department.  I just wanted to let all the Gateway computer users 
out there know that we've discovered the solution for the 'Jumpy mouse' 
problem in 'Aegis, Guardian of the fleet' and 'Jutland'.

It turns out that Gateway has a new BIOS chip which fixes the problem.  
They were good enough to send us several machines to work with, but as 
Murphey's law would have it none of those machines exibited the problem.  
Well, it seems that the new BIOS chip fixes it right up.

So if you're having the problem where your mouse seems to jump in 8 or 16 
pixel increments then give Gateway's Tech support a call and they can 
help you out.  Thanks.



